course: dictionary
lesson: 8374
title: Roux: a word from the kitchen
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which meaning is right. «Melt the butter, stir in the flour to make a roux, then add the milk slowly.» Here a roux is something you cook, so it must be a mixture of butter and flour.
explain: The same word can mean something quite different in another sentence. Roux is also a French word meaning reddish-brown, and it is a French surname too. Ask yourself: is the sentence about food, a colour, or a person's name?
explain: French words come with their own clues. «A girl with dark hair is brune, and ginger hair is roux or rousse, never rouge.» The sentence is about hair, so roux and rousse describe colour, not cooking. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: A roux is a mixture of melted butter (or fat) and flour, cooked together.
fact: A roux is used to thicken sauces, soups and gravy.
fact: In French, roux means reddish-brown, and «rousse» means ginger hair.
fact: In French, «brune» means dark-haired, so the word for hair tells you the colour.
fact: In Cajun and Creole cooking from Louisiana, a dark roux gives flavour to gumbo.
exercise: «Melt the butter, stir in the flour to make a roux, then add the milk slowly.» What is a roux? | A type of macaroni | *A mixture of melted butter and flour | A dark-haired girl | A kind of milk
exercise: In Louisiana cooking, a dark roux gives flavour to which dish? | *Gumbo | Chocolate cake | Toast | Fish and chips
exercise: «A girl with dark hair is brune, and ginger hair is roux or rousse, never rouge.» What does rousse mean? | A cooking sauce | Dark-haired | *Ginger, a hair colour | Bright red, painted on
test: «Stir the roux until it turns golden.» What does roux mean here? | A French surname | *A cooking mixture of butter and flour | A French city | Reddish-brown hair
test: Which French word means dark-haired? | *Brune | Rousse | Rouge | Roux
exam: In «Make a roux, then add the milk slowly», what does roux mean? | A reddish-brown colour | A French surname | *A mixture of melted butter and flour | A dark-haired girl
